SUMMARY:WAVES VIENNA: WORLD NEWS (UK) / SADSVIT (UA) / CHEST. (FR)VERA DAISIES (FR) (Uhrzeit prüfen)
LOCATION:Chelsea
DESCRIPTION:Doors: 18:15   VERA DAISIES (FR) – 18:30 Former member of the duo Ottis Cour\, Vera Daisies launches her solo project: a raw and incandescent indie rock\, where grunge\, pop\, and shoegaze blend with sharp\, melodic songwriting. After opening for The Libertines\, Tess Parks\, and the London band Sorry\, she unveils her ?rst EP "Clever Girl in January 2026\, which reveal the different shades of her project. She turns heartbreak and disillusion into cries of emancipation\, sketching a universe where her illustrations constantly converse with the sound\, carried by a raw\, uncompromising energy.  www.instagram.com/veradaisies/?hl=de    chest. (FR) – 19:45 French band chest. formed at Paris’ Supersonic\, where Nicolas\, Pierre-Louis\, Thibault\, Alexis and Elliot connected through their work at the venue and shared love of loud rock’n’roll and sonic experimentation. Their sound blends abrasive\, melodic noise rock with electronic music\, drawing on British in?uences as well as industrial\, techno and shoegaze. Known for their energetic live shows\, irony and self-deprecating humour\, chest. were named by NME among the “100 artists to watch in 2025.” Their debut EP All Good Things End  (Howlin Banana) was released in February 2025\, followed by shows with DITZ\, Jehnny Beth\, Heavy Lungs and KNIVES\, and appearances at La Maroquinerie\, Rock en Seine and Eurosonic Noorderslag. In autumn 2025\, they began recording their debut album at Studio La Frette\, expanding their sound design and layered textures while staying rooted in their powerful\, melodic noise rock. www.instagram.com/chest.band/?hl=de    SADSVIT (UA) - 21:00 SadSvit is a 22-year-old Ukrainian artist who has become one of the de?ning voices of the new wave of Eastern European post-punk. His music – synth-driven\, melancholic – captures what it means to be young and Ukrainian right now. That emotional weight found its natural home in the of?cial S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2 soundtrack\, where six of his tracks appear. His song  "Kaseta" went viral in 2022 after defenders of Mariupol used it in a frontline video. Post Impreza wrote: "His tracks drift somewhere between a ?rst love and the news of another strike." On stage with a band\, that intimacy scales. www.instagram.com/sadsvit/?hl=de    WORLD NEWS (UK) – 22:15 World News draw from '70s and '80s post-punk\, indie-rock and shoegaze to craft atmospheric guitar riffs with nonchalant\, seductive melodies. Moody\, punchy and nostalgic\, they've drawn comparisons to The Smiths\, The Clash and Dire Straits — wearing nostalgia on their sleeve while remaining strangely original. 2024 brought two standout EPs (Escape and Mindsnap)\, a US debut at The New Colossus Festival in NYC\, and features in Stereogum's 40 Best New Artists and The Fader's 13 Artists to Watch for 2025. Singles 'Don't Want to Know' and 'Everything Is Coming Up Roses' set the tone for their 2026 debut LP \, alongside sell-out UK shows and summer festival dates. www.instagram.com/worldnewsgram/?hl=de  www.wavesvienna.com/  Tickets: www.universe.com/events/waves-vienna-2026-tickets-3KLWXG
